380: \item \textbf{Optional single precision on GPU (proposed).} \code{float32} doubles memory throughput; it should be sufficient for avalanche statistics, but must be validated against \code{float64} in one case before adoption;
381: \item \textbf{Adaptive time step in the overdamped regime (proposed; investigate cautiously).} With $Q \ll 1$, the dynamics is slow and $\Delta t$ tied to $T_0$ is conservative. A larger step, limited by the viscous scale, could reduce the cost of the slowest runs. This requires a dedicated convergence study before adoption. With the V40 gain, it is no longer a priority.
