165: \subsection{Phase 6 --- from tool to research (18/06 and 04/07)}
166: 
167: With the instrument mature, the focus shifted to science:
168: 
169: \begin{enumerate}
170: \item \textbf{Literature review}, detailed in Section~\ref{sec:pesquisa}, identifying the gap and study design;
171: \item \textbf{Publication strategy}, including ACS journals, the CAPES agreement, and high-impact alternatives;
172: \item \textbf{\code{--make\_images} (V39)}: it was found that, even without \code{--video}, the program unconditionally generated 4--5 summary PNG images per run. This cost is negligible in large arrays, but dominant in small arrays used for sweeps. The new parameter suppresses all image generation while preserving data CSVs, with a measured speedup of $\sim 3\times$ in small runs (2.03~s $\to$ 0.65~s for an $8\times8$ array);
173: \item \textbf{Campaign infrastructure}: the scripts \code{damping\_sweep.py} (orchestration of damping~$\times$~seed~$\times$~geometry sweeps, calling the simulator programmatically) and \code{damping\_sweep\_analysis.py} (full statistical analysis), both validated end to end (Section~\ref{sec:campanha});
174: \item \textbf{Performance optimizations implemented (04/07)}: the precomputed dipolar tensor (\textbf{V40}) and campaign parallelization with incremental \emph{manifest} and resume support (\code{damping\_sweep} V02). Details and measurements are in Section~\ref{sec:melhorias}. The measured V40 speedup is \textbf{35--45$\times$} per run, reducing the full campaign from $\sim$7--8~h to $\sim$15~min on a single core;
175: \item \textbf{New field protocols and refinements (V41--V45)}: hysteresis with log-symmetric spacing; pulse with explicit timing ($\Delta t$ + $t_{\mathrm{pulse}}$ + torque equilibrium); step modes \code{step\_pos}/\code{step\_neg}; \code{--t\_sim\_full} flag (run to the end without early stopping); halos also in the comparison figure (V43); a two-line live progress panel (V44); and hysteresis video with a dual panel, needles and evolving $M\times H$ curve side by side (V45). All legacy modes were validated as bit-identical.
176: \end{enumerate}
